      <div type="clause" n="20.3a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 20.3a</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="20.3a" corresp="#wit-hk">E puis seient tuz les vilains en franc plege.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk">And further all villeins shall be in frankpledge.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="507"><ref target="clause:WlArt_8">Wl art 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. Wl art. 8</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
